+# USDC Payouts
+
+Send USDC payouts to teammates and contributors on **Base**, with every payout recorded onchain and
+shown in a live feed.
+
+Built with [Scaffold-ETH 2](https://scaffoldeth.io) (Hardhat flavor): NextJS, RainbowKit, Wagmi, Viem
+and TypeScript.
+
+## How it works
+
+- `Payouts.sol` (`packages/hardhat/contracts`) pulls USDC from the sender with `transferFrom` and
+  emits a `Paid(from, to, amount, memo)` event.
+- The `/payouts` page walks the user through connect → switch to Base → approve USDC → send, and
+  renders the `Paid` feed.
+- USDC itself is an external contract, registered in `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`.
+
+| Contract | Network     | Address                                      |
+| -------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |
+| Payouts  | Base (8453) | `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2` |
+| USDC     | Base (8453) | `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` |
+
+> [!WARNING]
+> **The Payouts address above has no contract code on Base.** `eth_getCode` returns `0x` from three
+> independent Base RPCs, and Basescan reports the address as unverified with no source. There is also
+> no `packages/hardhat/deployments/` record in this repo, so the deploy was never captured here.
+>
+> Until `Payouts` is actually deployed to Base and `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`
+> is regenerated with the real address, every payout will fail at simulation. This must be resolved
+> before shipping:
+>
+> ```
+> yarn deploy --network base
+> yarn verify --network base
+> ```
 
 ## Requirements
 
-Before you begin, you need to install the following tools:
-
 - [Node (>= v20.18.3)](https://nodejs.org/en/download/)
 - Yarn ([v1](https://classic.yarnpkg.com/en/docs/install/) or [v2+](https://yarnpkg.com/getting-started/install))
 - [Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads)
 
-## Quickstart
-
-To get started with Scaffold-ETH 2, follow the steps below:
-
-1. Install dependencies if it was skipped in CLI:
+## Local development
 
 ```
-cd my-dapp-example
 yarn install
+yarn chain     # local Hardhat network (terminal 1)
+yarn deploy    # deploy Payouts (terminal 2)
+yarn start     # NextJS app on http://localhost:3000 (terminal 3)
 ```
 
-2. Run a local network in the first terminal:
-
-```
-yarn chain
-```
+Run the contract tests with `yarn hardhat:test`.
 
-This command starts a local Ethereum network using Hardhat. The network runs on your local machine and can be used for testing and development. You can customize the network configuration in `packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts`.
+## Environment variables
 
-3. On a second terminal, deploy the test contract:
+Copy `packages/nextjs/.env.example` to `.env.local` and fill in:
 
-```
-yarn deploy
-```
+| Variable                                | Required in production | Purpose                                                                |
+| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL`              | **Yes**                | Dedicated Base RPC. Without it the app falls back to a rate-limited public endpoint. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | **Yes**                | Own WalletConnect project ID; the scaffold default is shared and throttled. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY`           | Recommended            | Used for ENS/price lookups on mainnet.                                 |
 
-This command deploys a test smart contract to the local network. The contract is located in `packages/hardhat/contracts` and can be modified to suit your needs. The `yarn deploy` command uses the deploy script located in `packages/hardhat/deploy` to deploy the contract to the network. You can also customize the deploy script.
+These must be set on the host (Vercel/system env config), not just in the repo.
 
-4. On a third terminal, start your NextJS app:
+## Deploying
 
 ```
-yarn start
+yarn deploy --network base
+yarn verify --network base     # verify on Basescan after every deploy
+yarn vercel:yolo --prod        # frontend
 ```
-
-Visit your app on: `http://localhost:3000`. You can interact with your smart contract using the `Debug Contracts` page. You can tweak the app config in `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts`.
-
-Run smart contract test with `yarn hardhat:test`
-
-- Edit your smart contracts in `packages/hardhat/contracts`
-- Edit your frontend homepage at `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx`. For guidance on [routing](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/routing/defining-routes) and configuring [pages/layouts](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/routing/pages-and-layouts) checkout the Next.js documentation.
-- Edit your deployment scripts in `packages/hardhat/deploy`
-
